#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9460289-3e48-558e-b149-3e12a25e50a6" :knowledge-point/title "Flipping the Sign of an Inequality in a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d0891c-161c-5834-b9eb-6586cb0c9bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\in [-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566446} {:answer/id #uuid "51695b2b-00d2-5afd-9514-8c7464cb7b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\in (1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566517} {:answer/id #uuid "82ae7df2-949d-5f30-8f35-50b577c6c509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566612} {:answer/id #uuid "ed75b313-51b7-5ed1-ad30-3536875d859b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\in [-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566844} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a0d75b-e243-5815-8927-4c35ba1889f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\in [-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a0d75b-e243-5815-8927-4c35ba1889f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\in [-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566859} :answer-field/id #uuid "f016f7be-fb1c-5a42-bf74-e51c3d868c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e2e4815-0beb-5581-be50-52ebe618cd02" :question/math-academy-id "q-156127" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}n+2<5 \\\\ 1-2n\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $n$ that satisfy both $n+2<5$ and $1-2n\\le 3$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $n+2<5\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n+2 & <5 \\\\ n+2-2 & <5-2 \\\\ n & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/4e/4e6e1c1a65abf5b7b88d39bb4d2606d64d5bc9ae526925e9f869eab0927194e3.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-2n\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2n & \\le 3 \\\\ 1-2n-1 & \\le 3-1 \\\\ -2n & \\le 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2n) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2n & \\ge -2 \\\\ \\frac{2n}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ n & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8e/8e96c91b84e3c69b2e8f58251dbe21294ef8b23ffa695c1b7fbe53ad4f22b2fc.png)\n\nTo find the values of $n$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/cd/cd1d2ad0e357eb3117e5b61351afeda01a348bfff5aec1a2d2940c77ecae120c.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $n\\in [-1,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f83060-457e-51bb-a48c-880d80b51fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566384} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7f2bd0-2eb9-577c-8ebe-c9c59314df42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (3,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566454} {:answer/id #uuid "62a7710c-4104-514f-9c9a-a23045e79c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566553} {:answer/id #uuid "941d31e7-a180-5faa-b9a0-cad9aa59b9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (1,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566652} {:answer/id #uuid "c2287c90-b752-5994-8a09-4fd688b59847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "941d31e7-a180-5faa-b9a0-cad9aa59b9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (1,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566652} :answer-field/id #uuid "1afdbe50-eaa8-50d5-ae52-c02ad59c8fa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6919ce13-e2d9-594d-bb7b-2bdd566b01d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-156128" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $1<2x-1\\le 5$ and $1-2x\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $1<2x-1\\le 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <2x-1\\le 5 \\\\ 1+1 & <2x-1+1\\le 5+1 \\\\ 2 & <2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{2} & <\\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ 1 & <x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/2b/2b111554de3019b78a3d6e8992477bb1401a53d7c2bbe09a6407e675b8d06daa.png)\n\n- Then, we solve  $1-2x\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x & \\le 3 \\\\ 1-2x-1 & \\le 3-1 \\\\ -2x & \\le 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2x) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2x & \\ge -2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ca/ca4d8a229772ec9d22a45c99cdad22379b6b55aa5d6fe4bb6288fe66d8c5696a.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/74/74cc11cbd20e5b82171d4c89407f24eb6f60ee558bf41a313009839c6f885f7e.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $x\\in (1,3].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f6f04e-ecce-5318-b72b-46478661ced0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Systems of Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "916544ca-e729-52f9-99f7-464a605534c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "916544ca-e729-52f9-99f7-464a605534c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566649} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c5013c-7ef7-5aa3-9cbc-e11a67222488" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad0c248c-2575-5291-8824-399e68cd193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad0c248c-2575-5291-8824-399e68cd193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566707} :answer-field/id #uuid "53abe454-b2dd-5ad2-8fe1-b231d8cd91f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3df23fd-8dd2-5adf-999f-c1d609ac0517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3df23fd-8dd2-5adf-999f-c1d609ac0517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566751} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8fccfc7-d496-5162-8471-a2686b179c57" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2b2b02a-ff73-57d9-825a-216db2bab95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-208784" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y-5\\le 2 \\\\ 2y+7>11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$y\\le $\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $y$ that satisfy both $y-5\\le 2$ and $2y+7>11$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $y-5\\le 2\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & \\le 2 \\\\ y-5+5 & \\le 2+5 \\\\ y & \\le 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b0/b0107bec7ccb2c56036de405a29870e8cfcc166cc6405f425fc3296ec8f1be2b.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $2y+7>11\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+7 & >11 \\\\ 2y+7-7 & >11-7 \\\\ 2y & >4 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & >\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ y & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/59/59523e51144ef776295ec43032def1bc0192351deb6294fbb2d56acd87bb2cac.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $y$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/98/981477f5336b96998b61b7ab18647609cb33c12984c14049621ac15c698c25a5.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $2<y\\le 7.$"}]}
